{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And all the families of the earth shall be blessed through you, etc.</b> For so we find in Aram that they were blessed through him, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 70), and this is their language: that before Jacob came, they were hard-pressed for water, and once he arrived they were blessed with water. And likewise also in Egypt, from the time he descended, the decree of famine was annulled, and they were blessed on his account." "And the verse's saying <b>and through your seed</b> [means] that all the while the Holy Temple stood, the blessing of the seventy nations and their sustenance was through the instrumentality of Israel, for they would offer seventy bulls on the festival (Sukkah 55b), and in the exiles as well the sustenance of the nations and their leaning upon Israel, as it is written (Song of Songs 1:6): ״שָׂמוּנִי נוֹטֵרָה אֶת הַכְּרָמִים״ etc." "<b>By way of</b> remez, the entire portion alludes to the matter of man, as our Sages of blessed memory began to say regarding it (Zohar vol. 1, 147a): <b>And Jacob went out</b> — this is the soul upon its departure from the supernal world, and it is called Jacob on account of the evil impulse that clings to its heels." "And the verse's saying <b>from Be'er Sheva</b> — the place from which souls emerge is called a well of living waters, and <b>Sheva</b> alludes to the oath of HaShem that the soul swears upon its departure, that it shall not transgress a word of Torah (Niddah 30b)." "And the verse's saying <b>and he went toward Haran</b> — according to what our Sages of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 91b), that the evil impulse enters a person upon his departure from his mother's womb, as it is written (Genesis 4:7): ״לַפֶּתַח״ etc." "And the verse's saying <b>וַיִּפְגַּע בַּמָּקוֹם</b> — for a person must pray to HaShem, who is the מָקוֹם (Place) of the world, that He not abandon him to his own hand." "And the verse's saying <b>וַיָּלֶן שָׁם כִּי בָא הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ</b> — that one must conduct himself thus until departing from this world when his sun sets, and this is what they said, of blessed memory (Avot 2:4): ״אַל תַּאֲמֵן בְּעַצְמְךָ עַד יוֹם מוֹתְךָ״." "And the verse's saying <b>וַיִּקַּח מֵאַבְנֵי הַמָּקוֹם</b> follows what they said, of blessed memory (Berakhot 5b), and this is their language: Rabbi Shimon ben Lakish said, a person should always arouse the good inclination, etc., and if not, let him engage in Torah, as it is written (Psalms 4:5): ״אִמְרוּ בִלְבַבְכֶם״. And this is the verse's saying ״מֵאַבְנֵי הַמָּקוֹם״ — meaning, the building of the world, which is words of Torah. Also, one may connect to them the stones of the place with which the evil inclination and its forces are stoned and condemned, and this is what they said, of blessed memory (Sotah 21a): Torah protects from the evil inclination both at a time when one engages in it and at a time when one does not engage in it." "And the verse's saying <b>וַיָּשֶׂם מְרַאֲשֹׁתָיו</b> is to be understood along the lines of what Rabbi Shimon ben Lakish said: if he did not prevail — let him recite Keri'at Shema upon the bed, as it is said: ״עַל מִשְׁכַּבְכֶם״ (Psalms 4:5)." "And the verse's saying <b>וַיִּשְׁכַּב בַּמָּקוֹם הַהוּא</b> alludes to what Rabbi Shimon ben Lakish concluded: if he did not prevail — let him remind himself of the day of death. And this is the verse's saying <b>וַיִּשְׁכַּב</b> — the known lying down <b>בַּמָּקוֹם</b> the known place, the way of all the earth, the house of appointment for all the living." "And after all these conditions, he is assured that he will vanquish the evil inclination, and from now on the verse announces to him that he will be worthy of being a branch of the branches of prophecy — that HaShem would reveal Himself to him, and speak to him in a dream. Go out and learn from the dreams of R. Elazar ben Arakh, cited in the book of the Zohar (part 1, 139b; and in Zohar Ḥadash, Lekh Lekha 25a)." "And the ladder is the sod of a person's soul. And since upon the soul's departure from a person when he lies down to sleep it is not utterly uprooted from the person's body — rather, a part of it remains in the body — this is what the verse means by <b>set on the earth</b> (i.e., its base), while a part <b>reaches to heaven</b>. And the proof of this is that when a person is asleep he can be awakened by the movement of the sleeping body; if the person's soul had departed and gone on its way, it would not sense the body's movement. Rather, it is certainly <b>set on the earth</b> while <b>its top reaches to heaven</b> — meaning there is no barrier between it and the heavens. Since the evil inclination in the person is nonexistent (ayin), the soul reaches to heaven." "And the verse's saying <b>angels of Elohim ascending</b>, etc., alludes to the aspect of good deeds in which a person engages in this world, through which he draws supernal lights into the root of their souls — and these are called, in the words of the Sages of blessed memory (Zohar part 1, 18a), 'mayin nukvin (feminine waters).' To them the name 'angels of Elohim' is applied. And so it is in Mishnat Ḥasidim (Avot, chapter 4): one who performs a single mitzvah acquires for himself one advocate (proklit). And upon the ascent of these, 'mayin dekhurin (masculine waters)' descend — for through the arousal of the lower waters, the supernal waters are aroused to pour awesome lights into the sod of his soul. This is what the verse means by <b>descending upon it.</b>" "And the verse's saying <b>and behold, YHWH stood</b> — meaning, from this level he will ascend to prophecy itself: not speaking to him in a dream, but the Shekhinah would be revealed upon him. And accordingly you will find that the Sages of blessed memory said (Rambam, Laws of Repentance, chapter 5) regarding Israel that not one of them was deprived of prophecy, and all are fit for this matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:46.633875134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}